# Luminary marker — cli#254 sub-steps 5+6 (Docker wire)
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: feat/254-docker-wire
- lead: michael-nygard
- supporting: [john-ousterhout, linus-torvalds]
- rationale:
  - lead (Nygard) — stability pattern. Adopters run Docker CI on every
    PR. Interactive drive step adds new failure modes (expect timeout,
    missing token, network drop on gh close). Every one must fail-soft
    with a specific exit code, not a generic crash. Nygard's lens
    verifies the ship at Step 5.5.
  - supporting (Ousterhout) — deep module. The new function
    `_docker_harness_run_v2_interactive` hides all interactive-drive
    orchestration behind one call. main() sees a single exit code from
    the whole batch.
  - supporting (Linus) — adopter contract. Existing adopters on older
    cli versions (no smoke-drive-generic.sh) must still get GREEN CI.
    New step skips cleanly on missing prereqs.
- balancing-check-role: Nygard confirms fail-soft coverage across all
  new failure modes before Step 6 merge.
